{"id": "EUVD-2026-107021", "enisaUuid": "5a880756-0365-307e-a854-b2264c4922ff", "description": "Trigger.dev 4.5.0 before 4.6.0 contains an information disclosure vulnerability in the Dashboard Agent input proxy that stores a delegated user-actor token in browser-readable session input records. Attackers holding a chat's public session token can read the in records endpoint to recover the token from payload.metadata.userActorToken and replay it for environment JWT exchange.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:50:25", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/triggerdotdev/trigger.dev/security/advisories/GHSA-wpp9-mq73-fhqm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trigger-dev-4.5.0-before-4.6.0-dashboard-agent-user-token-disclosure-via-session-records"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114070", "GHSA-8hxg-26q3-8q8c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ce29e234-2bec-3f56-8a7f-9d9cda279d20", "product": {"name": "trigger.dev", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}, "product_version": "4.5.0 <4.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3d7c6884-9462-3d8e-8474-bc06e6721779", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}], "isExploited": false}